Customer Churn Data Cleaning & Preprocessing
An end-to-end, reproducible data cleaning and validation pipeline designed for customer churn datasets using Python and Pandas.  
This project establishes a standardized ETL (Extract, Transform, Load) workflow to clean raw customer data, enforce data types, sanitize categorical values, verify business logic rules, and perform mathematical validations prior to downstream analytics or machine learning.  
Executive Summary
Raw data collected from production databases and billing systems often contains subtle formatting issues, such as un-trimmed categorical whitespaces, non-standardized column names (camelCase vs. space-separated), loose data typing, and floating-point total charge discrepancies.  
This pipeline automates the sanitization process using standard data engineering patterns to ensure the resulting dataset is consistent, clean, and fully validated.  
Key Technical Achievements
Automated Schema Standardization: Automatically converts column headers containing spaces, camelCase, or special characters into standardized snake_case using regular expressions.  
Pandas 3.x Modern Compliance: Built using explicit data type inclusions (select_dtypes(include=["object", "string"])) to prevent deprecation warnings across modern Pandas versions.  
Mathematical Business Rule Auditing: Validates financial integrity by mathematically confirming that recorded total charges equal monthly charges multiplied by customer tenure ($Total = Monthly \times Tenure$) within floating-point tolerances.  
Data Quality Audit Reporting: Generates a real-time summary report tracking total rows, column counts, missing value checks, duplicate counts, and constraint validations.  
